---------------
 README lctlib
---------------
Veronika Gayler, July 2009

The landcover library is edited as an OpenDocument spreadsheet (lctlib.ods).
It includes different sheets:

  nlct11     - corresponds to the lctlib used with the dynamic vegetation 
  nlct14     - corresponds to the lctlib used in millennium expriments
  nlct14C3C4 - as nlct14, however C3 and C4 crops are considered

  nlct21     - merge of the above three lctlibs. Different numbers are used for
               the LCTclasses.

The idea is not to change any of the LCTs listed on nlct19, but to rather add
new lct classes. This allows the usage old initial files with future LCT
libraries.

Export from the staroffice document
-----------------------------------

File -> Save as -> "Text CSV"
    (x) Edit filter settings
    Save

Klick "Yes" to save in Text CVS even though formatting might get lost 

Chose field options:
  Character set Unicode (UTF-8)
  Field delimiter {space}
  Text delimiter "
 (x) Save cell content as shown
  And klick "OK"


Convert the csv text file to the lctlib.def
-------------------------------------------

tr -d '"' < lctlib.csv > lctlib_nlct21.def 
 
